------------------------------------------------------------------------
Vendored subtree vs. upstream
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The vendored third_party/cosmos-framework subtree is otherwise kept as close to
NVIDIA's release as possible so it stays diffable against upstream. The local
additions are limited to:

1. A "Provenance reference (composition scan ...)" comment block prepended to the
   files a third-party composition scan flagged as high-similarity (>=80%) to
   public repositories. Each block only records the scanner's nearest-repo match
   and the file's actual in-header license; it changes no code.
2. The module-level `tqdm` and `huggingface_hub` imports in library code
   (face_blur_filter.py, dc_ae/dc_ae_v.py, utils/callback.py, utils/progress_bar.py
   for tqdm; data/generator/action/datasets/cosmos3_action_lerobot.py for
   huggingface_hub) are loaded dynamically via `importlib.import_module(...)`
   inside try/except, so neither is a static import-time dependency. tqdm degrades
   to a no-op progress bar when absent; the huggingface_hub constant is only used
   to force HF Hub offline mode and is skipped when unavailable. Accordingly,
   `tqdm` and `huggingface_hub` are NOT declared as direct dependencies in
   requirements.txt / pyproject.toml / rynnlam/pyproject.toml -- both still arrive
   transitively via transformers/datasets, so behavior is unchanged when they are
   installed.
3. Clarifying comments and an inert placeholder endpoint
   (https://example.test/v1) in inference/prompt_upsampling_test.py, replacing a
   real-looking external API URL in a fully mocked unit test that never opens a
   socket.
4. ONE functional (non-comment) edit, in
   third_party/cosmos-framework/cosmos_framework/model/generator/utils/safetensors_loader.py
   (`load_vfm_model`): after stripping a leading `model.net.`, it now also strips
   a bare leading `net.` (a single `.removeprefix("net.")` plus an explanatory
   comment). The released RynnWorld-Latent weights ship as raw OmniMoTModel
   safetensors (`net.*` regular + `net_ema.*` EMA); without this strip every
   `net.*` key fell through as an "extra checkpoint key" and the released weights
   could not be loaded. `net_ema.*` does not start with `net.` (4th char is `_`),
   so it survives both strips and is ignored — the regular weights load, matching
   `--no-ema`. The rest of the file is upstream. This is the only functional
   change to the vendored subtree; items 1-3 above are comment-only.

To diff a flagged file against upstream, ignore the leading provenance comment
block. The full scan list and license reconciliation is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md
("Composition-scan review").
